 "texts": [
  "The dark swallows will return to your balcony to hang their nests again and will calling playing again to their glass with the wing.",
  "The dark swallows will return to your balcony their nests to hang, and again flapping their wings calling.",
  "The dark swallows will return to their nests, and with their wing will again play among the glass, calling all the time.",
  "The dark swallows will return to your balcony to hang their nests, and again listening to the flute.",
  "The dark swallows will return again to his balcony their nests to hang, and one more time with his wing to his glasses they will play by calling.\nTranslation Notes: The core of this poem actually revolves around the idea of how despite being of different types, species, and color all living beings, including nature, converge in repressing the threatening dark with the sky. So, while nature-like the birds which are the central image of the poem-also experience the darkening and the approaching of dark (it's represented by two sets of wings and singing), they don't fall into the",
  "The dark, return starlings to your veranda their nests to hang, and once again with their wing to its glass roar will call each.",
  "The dark swallows will return to your balcony their nests to hang, and with their wing again playing on your glasses will call.",
  "They will return the dark swallows on their balcony with their nests to hang, and again with the wing to their mirrors playing they will call.",
  "Will come back the dark swallows in its balconies to hang her nests, and again with their wings folds to prancing their windows will call.",
  "Dark swallows will return to your balcony to hang their nests again, and again call their glasses playing with their wings.",
  "The dark swallows will return to build their nests on your balcony again, and with their wings playing with your windows they will call again.",
  "They will return the dark swallows their nests to hang in your balcony, and once again with their wings to their window games playing calling.",
  "The dark swallows will return to their balcony, dipping their wings like kissing birds and their music playing as they come closer to call your name.",
  "The dark swallows will return to their nests to hang on your balcony, and will play again with its wings will call to its windows.",
  "The dark swallows, tired of fly away, are back to nest on your balcony balcony. Their wings play, swing, in the windows.",
  "The dark swallows will return to their nests hanging on your balcony, and again calling to your glass with their wing.",
  "The dark swallows will return their nests to your balcony, and other times with the wing to its windows playing will call.",
  "The dark swallows will return to hang their nests on your balcony, and again, playing with your glass, they will call.",
  "Dark swallows will return to hang their nests on your balcony, and once again calling like they play with their glasses on their wings.",
  "Returning dark starlings to your balcony their nests to hang, and again with their wings to their glass to play, they will call will call.",
  "Your balcony will once again nest the dark swifts\nWill again call with wing to your glass-playing.",
  "The dark swallows will return to your balcony their nests to hang, and again with their wings to your windows will call.",
  "The stealthy swallows will return in spring, nest beneath the eaves, with their beady eyes shining, calling as they please.​",
  "The dark swallows will return to their nest in your balcony, and again with their wing to their windows round and round they will come calling.",
  "The dark swallows will return to your balcony, their nests to hang, and again with the wing to their glass playing they will call.",
  "They'll come back to your balcony next year to hang their nests and call again with their wings nudding your windows.",
  "The black swallows will return to your balcony with their nests to hang. And once more flapping their wings at your windows calling.",
  "Swans will return to hang their nests on your balcony, and with their wings playing your windows, they will once again call.",
  "The dusky swallows will return to hang their nests on your balcony, and again with their wing calling on your windows.\n \nSpanish",
  "The dark swallows will return to their nest in your porch plate, and once again they will play with your windows clapping.",
  "The dark returning swallows in your balcony, with your shelter in the air throw it, and his wings throw it against the crystal, they will ring again.",
  "Back in your balcony will her dark martins come back with the string of their nest. And as usual they'll call you outdoors by knocking at your windows with their wings.",
  "The dark house martins will come back on the balcony to hand on their nests, and with their wings on your windows they will come to play.",
  "The dark swallows will return in your balcony to hang their nests again, and again they will play their wings in your windows calling.",
  "the dark swallows their nests will return to your balcony to hang, and again with his edge in your glass, they will call.",
  "The dark swallows will return to their nests under your balcony, playing with their wings on your windows, and once more they will call \"Zoo-Zoo-Zoo\".",
  "The dark swallows will return to their nest on your balcony, and again with their wings caressing the glass, they will cry out.",
  "Those dark swallows will rear their nests again in your balcony, and once again with their wing playing will sing.",
  "The dark swallows will return to your balcony their nests to hang, and again with the wing to their windows play they will call.",
  "Returning dark swifts in the tall will hang balcony their nests, and again with the wing to their glass calling will.",
  "The dark swallows will come back to your skylight to hang their nests, and again playing on the windows with the wing they will call.",
  "The dark swallows will return to hang their nests in your balcony again and this time, with the wing playing on their windows, they will call out again.",
  "The dark swallows will return to hanging their nests on your balcony, and another time, playing with their glasses, calling from the wing.",
  "Back on your balcony will come the dark swallows their nests to hang, and again with the wing to their glass crying playing.",
  "If you’re really here, then I would love to hear your voice! You smoked the best clove cigarettes, we always together smoked the best clove cigarettes, I would prefer you if you;’d stay, but whatever you want, whatever you want!\n(If you’re REALLY here, I’d love to hear your voice!)",
  "The dark swifts will return to hang their nests on your balcony and once again they will call to your windows playing with their wings.",
  "the dark swallows will return to their nest in your window and once again playing with our wings will knock on our crystal glass calling us.",
  "The dark swifts will be back on your balcony to hang their nests and again with wing whistling fly calling outside.",
  "The dark swallows will return to their nest to hang, and with their wing to your glass playing, will call again.",
  "The dark swallows will return to their nests to hang in your balcony and, with their wings to your windows, calling again.",
  "The dark swallows will once again return to your balcony to hang their nests, and again playing with your windows will call with their outstretched wings.",
  "The dark swallows will return to your balcony to hang their nests, and again with the wing to your windows calling.",
  "The dark swallows will return to your balcony to hang their nests again, and once again they will call while playing with your windows.",
  "The dark swallows will return to your balcony to hang their nests and again with the wing will call calling to the glass playing.",
  "The dark swallows will return to their nests hanging on your balcony, and after their wings playing their crystal will call again.",
  "<strong>Carneros al ala a sus cristales (llamarán)/ The dark swifts will come back to hang their nests in your balcony, and they will call again to play with glass wings.</strong>",
  "They will return to your balcony the dark swallows hollows and again with one thigh on their glasses playing they will call.",
  "The dark swallows will return to hang in your balcony their nests, and again flapping against the playing lights call with his wing.",
  "Your dark swallows will return cover to cover again your nests to hang, and again with the wing to your windows playing will call.",
  "Back will come the dark swallows their nests to hang, and another time with the wing to their bars calling will call.",
  "The dark swallows, that will return to the house by choirs to hang the its nests, and one more time to their glasses they will call, playing on their back wings.",
  "The dark swallows will fly back into your balcony with nests hanging from them. And once again they will take their wing to his windows, calling.",
  "Returning from their dark outing the swallows will hang their nests to your balcony swinging once again to your glass windows flapping.",
  "The dark swallows, they will return to your balcony their nests to hang, and they'll call with the wing, playing on their windows."
 ],
